Set errno when getlogin_r() can't get the user name.
If GetUserName() failed, getlogin_r() returned -1 without setting
errno, so logname's "getlogin" message showed whatever errno an earlier
call had left, or no reason at all. Set errno from the Windows error.

---
 win32/mingw.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -1575,6 +1575,7 @@
 	char *name;
 
 	if ( (name=get_user_name()) == NULL ) {
+		errno = err_win_to_posix();
 		return -1;
 	}
 
